    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "5fca8aead670b8006e2516cc",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/49b066ad8ea9ea30aa4e44fcf4c5f586?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FK-3.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/49b066ad8ea9ea30aa4e44fcf4c5f586?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FK-3.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/49b066ad8ea9ea30aa4e44fcf4c5f586?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FK-3.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/49b066ad8ea9ea30aa4e44fcf4c5f586?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FK-3.png"
      },
      "displayName": "kefo",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5fca8aead670b8006e2516cc",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>I wanted to add a comment here for two reasons:  1) to start resurfacing this issue and 2) to provide any background to what I've done in the past that may or may not be helpful.  Let's consider the 1st point covered.</p>\n\n<p>As for the 2nd point, when it comes to testing whether this issue exists, I basically wrote a script that traverses a repository, gathers all the URIs, and then performs a HEAD and GET request on each resource looking for a 200, 404 pattern respectively.  That's all it really is.  It's more or less a single python script so easy to distribute and use.  (I'll add that it is also possible, now, to perform a GET on each resource and tail the fcrepo.log, which now outputs INFO about each requested resource with a reference to a non-existent resource.)</p>\n\n<p>I don't know if the following idea is helpful, but it is something we've contemplated on our end to correcting this sooner rather than later.  We think we could simply perform a GET on each resource, strip the Fedora-specific properties, and PUT the resource back in the repo.  We've not moved on this beyond theoretical discussion, but I'd welcome any immediate thoughts on it.</p>\n\n\n",
